  "findings": [
    "Creature and player targets were requested and observed; the server echoed each requested GUID into A's UNIT_FIELD_TARGET, and `target 0` cleared it to 0x0.",
    "Malformed GUIDs (0xzz, 2^64, -1, 0x, empty, missing, 1.5, an extra argument) were refused at argument parsing with exit 1 and `invalid guid`; nothing was sent.",
    "Stale GUIDs were NOT refused at `target`: a never-observed made-up GUID, a player who had logged out, a dead creature and a despawned creature were all accepted and echoed by the server as A's target.",
    "Stale GUIDs were refused downstream by face-guid (target_not_observed or target_stale), walk-toward (target_not_observed) and fight (target_not_pve_creature or target_dead). attack and cast were accepted by the client as intent; the server refused the cast (result 12, SPELL_FAILED_BAD_TARGETS) and answered attack with SMSG_ATTACKSTOP.",
    "Suspected bug: SMSG_ATTACKSTOP without a victim (AzerothCore WorldSession::SendAttackStop(nullptr) for an unknown GUID) fails to parse in parseAttackStop (src/wow/protocol/combat.ts:35-41) with packet_error 'Out of bounds access', opcode 324; combat --json then kept pendingAttack set until stop-attack."
  ],
  "omittedFromSteps": [
    "01:53:10Z: `target 0` sent from a shell before a failed `goto 8745 -6600 60` (pick_destination: ambiguous ground column); session.log lines 140-142 show target_requested -> target_observed 0x0 in 282 ms, with the goto control_error between them.",
    "01:53:20Z-01:53:48Z: two `face`/`move forward` legs toward the Springpaw Stalker area stopped with height_unresolved after about 17 and 3.5 yd (session.log lines 143-161). A was never in combat and no creature attacked A."
  ],
